  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Say which harness you mean",
      "items": [
        "AAMAD is the build harness: nine persona contracts in .claude/agents/, three gated phases, one artifact per epic. It does not ship.",
        "The Claude Agent SDK is the runtime harness: triage-router delegating to order-specialist, returns-advisor, faq-policy, plus-specialist and escalation-handoff.",
        "The adapter is the only link between them, and it points one way: it shapes the generated app, it does not orchestrate AAMAD's phases."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Structural, not prompted",
      "items": [
        "Four independent layers keep money tools out: nothing bound in the process, a startup assertion that throws, an exact-set CI test that fails when a tool is added, and PreToolUse denial.",
        "Specialists cannot delegate because the Agent tool is absent from their tools array — not because a prompt forbids it.",
        "Hooks do the accounting: SubagentStart counts the hop, PostToolUse records the trace and tools_tried."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Two engines, one contract",
      "items": [
        "CHAT_ENGINE picks deterministic or sdk; both honour the same wire contract and the same escalation guarantee.",
        "The sdk engine is a dynamic import, so on the default path no key is read and no subprocess starts.",
        "That is what lets the same build run keyless in front of an audience."
      ]
    }
  ]
